{
  "quest.0A0A4FC4C933B5CC.title": "The Research Program",
  "quest.0752B5D72A823293.quest_desc": [
    "A stock rocket reaches orbit and nothing more. Modules, installed at the Upgrade tab, staying on the rocket through landings and rebuilds, are what make it a real ship.",
    "",
    "&6Cargo Module:&r hold grows from 1 row to 3. &6Autopilot:&r set a destination on the module, the ship flies itself and the lander stops cratering. &6Hydrogen Motor:&r swaps the engine from Fuel to Hydrogen, empty the tank first. &6Shield Module:&r heat shields on the hull.",
    "",
    "Most modules are crafted with desh, a Moon metal, or found in Moon Sphere chests. We will come back to this shelf after the first landing.",
  ],
  "quest.677608F2F0A93B44.title": "GET THIS THING OFF ME",
  "task.6E1A455DD4C07359.title": "Learn the rocket module catalog",
  "quest.44DF48BE87ACCC94.quest_desc": [
    "Pick &6Earth Orbit&r on the destination screen and the lander drops you into the thinnest place reachable: 0.5 gravity, minus 270 degrees, no air at all. The planet fills the sky below and nothing lives up here but what we bring.",
    "",
    "Go in a full suit with oxygen loaded, there is no ground to stand on either, until we make some. This black sky is the only place in the galaxy where a space station can be raised.",
  ],
  "quest.12058BED6DA0F944.quest_desc": [
    "Eight ingots to start, and that is only the beginning. The rocket body alone eats eight, and nearly every machine we build asks for a few more.",
    "",
    "Smelt Raw Titanium in a furnace or a blast furnace. While the metal runs, read ahead: plating blocks, slabs, stairs and pillars all exist for when a base deserves to look like a launch site.",
  ],
  "quest.5E451F5E0515D769.title": "Plating for the Pad",
  "quest.1AB510AAA30320FF.title": "Slay the Guardian",
  "task.2DDD02B8366FE5BA.title": "Run a sealed, oxygenated room on the Moon",
  "task.6C682968636A469D.title": "AllRightsReserved",
  "quest.36CCF8C0A1B62260.title": "The Split Machine",
  "quest.2673F444580FB511.title": "A Shell Worth Wearing",
  "quest.6687660A5F931460.quest_desc": [
    "The Company keeps a bounty ledger: kill one of each, a &6Lunar Parasite&r, a &6Luna Shadow&r from the forests, a &6Parasite Villager&r, its &6Evolved&r form, and even a &6Blue Fish&r for completeness.",
    "",
    "The evolved villager is the dangerous entry: an infection aura out to 4 blocks every 1.5 seconds, and attacks that apply Weakness and Slowness on top of the infection. Only the vaccine makes it safe.",
    "",
    "An official advancement confirms the full ledger.",
  ],
  "task.58F10D7631196A8C.title": "Read about the next world",
  "quest.0A599B4386B91DFB.quest_desc": [
    "Oil is not a block we dig up, it is a reserve hidden inside the chunk itself. Roughly one chunk in thirty-two holds a deposit, anywhere from 10 to 50,000 mB, and every deposit is &lfinite&r: once drained, it is gone.",
    "",
    "Lakes of oil also pool on the surface and underground while exploring, but the steady supply is the Pumpjack on a proven chunk. First we need the tool that sees underground.",
  ],
  "task.30BBCDD9881F8916.title": "Learn how the lander works",
  "quest.2045DBD6D4235282.quest_desc": [
    "The Moon has villages, standing structures where &6Aliens&r live and work. They take on a biome type and one of thirteen professions, and every profession runs its &lown trade table&r, different from anything an Earth villager offers.",
    "",
    "They are peaceful, they breed like villagers, they need no oxygen and they cannot catch the infection. Walk into a village and look around, the trade goods up here are worth the trip on their own.",
  ],
  "task.3C2D07F7A7BF4C68.title": "Confirm the program's milestones are done",
  "quest.1A84E9EE32AD3A1A.title": "The Room That Breathes",
  "quest.29DD1B7695C09410.title": "Dressing for the Vacuum",
  "quest.2CACC7F66C876699.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Lunar Blue Lake&r biome pools with a fluid that is definitely not water, the &6Blue Liquid&r. Schools of &6Blue Fish&r live in it happily, three to seven at a time, and they exist nowhere else.",
    "",
    "Scoop the liquid for later, it is one of the vaccine ingredients. The fish drop &6Blue Plasma&r, another vaccine ingredient and the heart of the Star Light Panel. Bring back one plasma now.",
  ],
  "quest.4CD31646E6B7D364.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Water Pump&r sits &ldirectly on top&r of a water source block, not beside it, not below it. Each cycle it swallows the source and stores 1,000 mB, then pushes water out of its top face into a pipe.",
    "",
    "Because the source is consumed, build it over an infinite spring so water flows back and the pump never runs dry. 100 FE per 1,000 mB pumped.",
  ],
  "quest.229852EBBD2B964A.title": "Learning to Fly",
  "quest.4D35E1719A092E9E.title": "Letting Go of the Stick",
  "quest.374FC20CBAA68FAB.quest_desc": [
    "This chapter runs on &2&lFlexible&r progression: tasks can gather progress before their quest unlocks, but a quest still only completes once its dependencies are done.",
    "",
    "Quests sitting off the main path are &boptional&r. They pay better stories than resources, and nothing downstream waits on them.",
    "",
    "",
    "&8&lNote:&r dimension visits and advancements only count once the quest is tracked by your book. If you already flew before opening this chapter, a couple of quests may ask for a fresh trip.&r",
  ],
  "quest.05071EBC1C9D0E2B.title": "Preflight Checklist",
  "quest.6F973629788228BA.quest_subtitle": "One bench, three workshops",
  "quest.05071EBC1C9D0E2B.quest_desc": [
    "Before the countdown, three things. &lFuel:&r the ship's tank holds 3,000 mB and each launch burns 1,000, a bucket or cell of Fuel in the fuel slot adds 1,000 at a time. &lClearance:&r the rocket refuses to start if anything blocks the air above the pad. &lCargo:&r whatever rides in the hold lands with you.",
    "",
    "Climb in and start the engine when ready, a 10-second countdown begins. At 400 blocks up, the destination screen opens and you pick a world.",
  ],
  "quest.6D7658B44ADF9D32.quest_desc": [
    "There is no live wire in this system, only pools. Generators, machines and power banks each store their own FE, and cables move charge from a fuller pool to an emptier one.",
    "",
    "That is why a base survives a generator outage, and why the fix for a slow base is never a thicker cable: it is more generation, or a bigger pool.",
  ],
  "quest.15961D434AF37681.title": "The Strong Generator",
  "quest.52860AE90D8D294A.quest_desc": [
    "The Moon: gravity 1.62, a sixth of home, and no atmosphere at all. Days run to +123°C, nights to -233, and the only air is what the helmet carries.",
    "",
    "AURA, the suit assistant, confirms touchdown and keeps an eye on you from here. Watch the jumps, everything falls slower, which is fun right up until the return trip makes Earth feel twice as heavy.",
    "",
    "Stay near the lander until the suit checks out. Then look up: this gray desert is the resource heart of the whole program.",
  ],
  "task.3A88F2FE55F92F31.title": "Survive a work session in open orbit",
  "quest.46C06EC4085C06DA.title": "Air Down the Hall",
  "quest.2FC0E94A3C2F4AD7.quest_subtitle": "Let's go!",
  "quest.16BF6F4CD96CDA92.quest_desc": [
    "The Tablet is the handbook the Company issues to every crew. Craft one from titanium nuggets, a glass pane and a titanium ingot, then right-click to open it.",
    "",
    "Inside: the full &6Wiki&r for every machine and mob, an &6SD Card&r reader for the logs left behind by earlier missions, a &6Planets&r app with gravity and atmosphere data, and &6Stats&r for the mission.",
    "",
    "Sneak-right-click a block, or drop an item on the tablet in your inventory, to jump straight to its page. When in doubt, look it up.",
  ],
  "quest.6CF267EBB35D9A3E.quest_desc": [
    "The earlier program left hardware all over Earth: crashed &6satellites&r, and &6operation bases&r that ran the quarantine effort. Their chests hold SD cards, tracking logs, command directives, the requisition notes for the honey shipments nobody understood.",
    "",
    "One base directive reads: keep the spores off Earth, keep the researchers alive. You can guess how both halves of that went.",
  ],
  "quest.6E978651BF338940.quest_subtitle": "Practice here, breathe there",
  "quest.4ECDD8F37D2492DF.title": "Ship With a Paint Job",
  "quest.6C561ECCEE2F268A.title": "Fuel for the Boots",
  "quest.421A0A4DA0A18F51.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Oxygen Module&r bolts onto the helmet and stores the air you will breathe: tier 1 holds 1,200 mB, tier 2 3,600, tier 3 6,000.",
    "",
    "At rest a player breathes 1 mB per second. Sprinting doubles that and jet flight quadruples it, so a long flight is paid for in air as well as fuel.",
    "",
    "Refill the helmet at an Oxygen Distributor, or pour in a fluid cell of oxygen held in hand. Breathing works underwater too.",
  ],
  "task.0F1468703FF801E7.title": "Trade with an Alien",
  "quest.169C28DB19A26128.quest_desc": [
    "You never land the rocket, a &6Lander&r forms around you at arrival and brings ship, fuel and cargo down as one package. It is a 30-slot container once it stops.",
    "",
    "&lWithout an autopilot it hits hard enough to dig a crater&r, land away from anything you care about. With an Autopilot Module installed, it sets down gently instead.",
    "",
    "Empty it by hand or let a Cargo Unloader pull everything out. And take the rocket back with you if the plan includes coming home.",
  ],
  "quest.1FBB699895BACDE6.title": "First Watts",
  "quest.421A0A4DA0A18F51.title": "Air on Your Back",
  "quest.2CBA0B7B5FB779D1.quest_desc": [
    "The Stellar Company is hiring crews again, and we signed up. The job: build a working space program out of a mine and a workbench, prospect for oil, refine fuel, assemble a rocket, and put boots on the Moon.",
    "",
    "This chapter is our flight plan. Follow the main line and every system gets explained one machine at a time. Side quests branch off the path; they are optional and never block the mission.",
    "",
    "Click a quest to read the briefing. Let's get to work.",
  ],
  "quest.4CD31646E6B7D364.title": "Tapping the Water",
  "quest.287BA93731FEC83F.title": "Reading the Enemy",
  "quest.532BADA61C869F51.title": "Canning the Kitchen",
  "quest.1A84E9EE32AD3A1A.quest_desc": [
    "Off Earth, open air does not exist: an unpressured space deals half a heart of damage every second to anything that breathes. The &6Oxygen Distributor&r fixes that one room at a time.",
    "",
    "Give it power and oxygen, by pipe from the electrolyzer or a cell in its slot, and it floods every walkable block with air, under three rules: the room must be &lcompletely sealed from the sky&r (glass roofs count), it must fit inside &l3x3 chunks&r, and it can hold at most &l50,000 blocks&r of air.",
    "",
    "Oxygen only drains per creature breathing - 1 mB each update. An empty room costs nothing but the 1 FE update.",
    "",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/stellaris/oxygen_distributor.png width:160 height:160 align:center}",
  ],
  "quest.538E11C948B4BB25.title": "Hard as Nails",
  "quest.4ECDD8F37D2492DF.quest_desc": [
    "Not every module is machinery. &6Skins&r repaint the hull, Galaxy, Frost or Military, and &6Rocket Models&r reshape the whole craft: Tiny, Small and Big.",
    "",
    "The tiny model is cheap, iron and a nose cone. Bigger silhouettes want titanium and desh. Purely cosmetic, completely worth it on launch day.",
  ],
  "quest.5D73AFF145322C4D.title": "Pour the Concrete",
  "quest.1AD93FB86F93CCB6.quest_desc": [
    "The recipe the research finally spells out: a &6Honey Bottle&r, a &6Blue Plasma&r from the lake fish, a &6Lunar Parasite Tooth&r, and a &6Lunar Crawler Spike Cluster&r, one part cure, three parts moon.",
    "",
    "Combine them in the Laboratory's &6Vaccine&r tab. The tooth drops from killed parasites about a fifth of the time; the spike cluster drops from the crawler mother and sits in her sphere's chests; the plasma comes off blue fish; the honey comes from home.",
  ],
  "quest.34920FBD01F40072.title": "Shadow on the Crater Wall",
  "quest.677608F2F0A93B44.quest_desc": [
    "&6Lunar Parasites&r spawn all over the Moon, more underground than on the surface, and they latch on. Once attached, one delivers the &6Infection&r: damage that lands at random, on no schedule, for as long as it lasts.",
    "",
    "There is no curing it with milk. The only way out is the vaccine, which is why the laboratory matters. If you get tagged, that is what this quest marks, and a reason to read ahead to the cure.",
    "",
    "Field note from the tunnels: they hunt by warmth and sound, honey burns them, cold slows them. Do not let them touch bare skin.",
  ],
  "quest.5E451F5E0515D769.quest_desc": [
    "A rocket does not launch off dirt. Eight &6Titanium Plating Blocks&r arranged in a ring become the launch pad, so forge them now and stash them away.",
    "",
    "The same plating comes in slabs, stairs and pillars, and later in desh and iron, if a hangar ever needs a floor that matches the ship.",
  ],
  "quest.292BE01E4FC2D031.title": "It Got Worse",
  "quest.421A0A4DA0A18F51.quest_subtitle": "The most important module in the galaxy",
  "quest.35D032B681A0C5F6.quest_desc": [
    "The planner's tooltip always lists what a station asks for. For the &6Small Station&r: 16 titanium blocks, 24 desh ingots, 12 silicon, 32 iron blocks, an antenna, 48 smooth quartz, 32 titanium plating and 32 glass. Medium roughly doubles it; Big triples the ambition.",
    "",
    "Desh comes from the Moon, a station is a project for &lafter&r the first landing, not before. Assemble the pile, plan the blueprint, and carry it up in the rocket's cargo.",
  ],
  "quest.0D8A53E286DEAA48.quest_desc": [
    "The Company's sky charts already paint &6Mars&r on the horizon, and the gravity manipulator even has a preset for it, but the flight corridor is not open. There is no Martian dimension in this build.",
    "",
    "Treat the red dot as a promise, not a destination. When the Company finishes the charts, this chapter will have somewhere new to point the rocket.",
  ],
  "quest.538133FC5D656547.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Pumpjack&r extracts oil wherever it stands inside a proven chunk, placement within the chunk does not matter. Power it, and it pulls 5 mB per tick at 2 FE per mB; its GUI shows how much is left below.",
    "",
    "Oil is pushed into any pipe or tank touching the machine, or drawn out with buckets and fluid cells.",
    "",
    "&lCareful when relocating:&r breaking a pumpjack returns everything except the drill head. Pick the spot once and let it work.",
    "",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/stellaris/pumpjack.png width:160 height:160 align:center}",
  ],
  "quest.169C28DB19A26128.title": "Landing Is the Hard Part",
  "quest.52DD11B192F6C7D9.quest_desc": [
    "The Moon is not one landscape but five: the Lunar Desert, the Moon Craters where most ruins stand, the Lunar Forest and the fire-scarred Burnt Forest, and the strange Lunar Blue Lake.",
    "",
    "Walk until you have stood in the forest and the crater field. The forest has its own wildlife, and none of it is friendly after dark.",
  ],
  "quest.664B2D0030C54D75.quest_desc": [
    "Not every ore comes out of a mine. Crashed &6meteorites&r scar the Overworld, and the largest impact sites hide veins of &6Novite&r, a metal no terrestrial rock contains.",
    "",
    "Smelt the raw chunks into ingots. Exactly one machine asks for them, and it only makes sense under a night sky with no air. Keep a few ingots for later.",
  ],
  "quest.52860AE90D8D294A.quest_subtitle": "The Moon",
  "quest.56240DD5B0414A39.quest_desc": [
    "The Moon is not empty. Its surface, lakes and ruins all have residents, some harmless, some very much not.",
    "",
    "The tablet's &6Wiki&r has a Mobs section with a 3D render of each of them; check it before picking a fight. The row of hunts below covers the ones you will meet.",
  ],
  "quest.5D73AFF145322C4D.quest_desc": [
    "Place the &6Rocket Launch Pad&r and the whole 3x3 platform builds at once; breaking the center takes it apart again.",
    "",
    "The pad accepts two upgrades, both installed by right-clicking its center: &6Launch Pad Towers&r for the full launch-day silhouette (they change nothing but the look, and they only exist as loot on the Moon), and an &6Antenna&r, which registers the pad as a landing waypoint.",
    "",
    "A Cargo Unloader next to the pad will empty the lander when a flight comes home.",
  ],
  "quest.6F973629788228BA.title": "The Engineering Station",
  "task.632C3F360E035BE0.title": "Use the Vaccine and gain permanent immunity",
  "quest.287BA93731FEC83F.quest_desc": [
    "Run the analyses until stage 4 unlocks, the point where the research names the last vaccine ingredient. Expect several full cells; every stage eats hundreds of parasites.",
    "",
    "Each stage also hands you an SD card. The cards from the lab tell the vaccine program's story better than any briefing, read them on the tablet between runs.",
  ],
  "quest.36862D1C576AB952.quest_subtitle": "Mission debrief",
  "quest.42AE42F63D04D8C7.quest_desc": [
    "The evacuation order mentions a transport that never cleared the pad, someone turned in the cargo hold and tore into the fuel lines. The &6destroyed spaceship&r still sits where it came down on the regolith.",
    "",
    "Walk the wreck with a weapon out: the dead ships spawn their own monsters. Whatever cargo was left is loot for whoever reads the black box.",
  ],
  "quest.04229666DE83F5D1.title": "Between Iron and Diamond",
  "quest.532BADA61C869F51.quest_desc": [
    "Outside breathable air you cannot swallow ordinary food at all, only a sealed &6Can&r. The &6Vacuumator&r makes them: food in the food slot, an empty can in the can slot, canned rations out.",
    "",
    "Keep feeding the same can until it fills, small cans hold 10 nutrition, big ones 20. Canning also condenses water out of the food (100 mB per can) into an internal tank that needs somewhere to go; the machine stops when it is full.",
    "",
    "Eating one takes two hands: hold the can and a drink, a water bottle works, then right-click.",
    "",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/stellaris/vacuumator.png width:160 height:160 align:center}",
  ],
  "quest.1AD93FB86F93CCB6.quest_subtitle": "Stage 4 complete",
  "task.31BA5662B5780115.title": "Meet the lunar wildlife",
  "quest.08D0F5470C27B89B.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Star Light Panel&r is the solar panel's night shift - 1 FE/t gathering starlight, producing exactly when solar goes idle. One of each keeps a base powered around the clock, and out here it is the only panel that makes sense at all.",
    "",
    "The recipe is the program's most exotic: blue plasma, desh and novite, one ingredient from the lake, one from the deep rock, one from a meteor crater back home.",
    "",
    "It also charges items in its slot like its twin.",
  ],
  "quest.03647D3F914AEF7A.quest_desc": [
    "Put the planned blueprint &lanywhere in the rocket's inventory&r, fly to Earth Orbit, and press &6Build Space Station&r. The structure raises itself around the landing site, a small station is still several rooms of hull.",
    "",
    "Every station arrives with an antenna already wired in, so it becomes a landing waypoint the moment it exists. The book cannot see the station go up, so check this off when you are standing inside it.",
  ],
  "quest.16BF6F4CD96CDA92.quest_subtitle": "Your best friend is a tablet",
  "quest.7714D18235F1B346.quest_desc": [
    "Open the Engineering Station's &6Rocket Station&r tab and lay out the ship: nose cone on top, eight titanium ingots for the hull, four fins at the sides, engine at the bottom.",
    "",
    "Take the rocket item out and the craft is yours. Right-click the center of the launch pad with it to stand the ship on the pad.",
  ],
  "quest.7FCD49FEAE1EAB87.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Night Vision Module&r goes in the helmet and sees in the dark on demand, a keybind toggles it.",
    "",
    "It runs off the helmet's battery, which means it competes with the Oil Finder module for charge and turns itself off when the battery runs flat. Charge the helmet in a power bank's item slot, and remember to charge before a cave survey.",
  ],
  "quest.78388E872EEB99B4.title": "AllRightsReserved",
  "quest.6CF267EBB35D9A3E.title": "Signals From Before",
  "quest.1E9E1E6667BB63BA.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Cargo Module&r triples the rocket's hold, two extra rows of inventory that ride down with you inside the lander.",
    "",
    "Crafted from desh, titanium and a chest, or pulled from Moon Sphere loot. It also fits the rover, where it adds the same two rows.",
  ],
  "quest.2CACC7F66C876699.title": "The Lake That Isn't Water",
  "quest.79CFFAB71C2DE2E3.title": "The Moon Metal",
  "quest.62857711BE7CB286.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Tier 1 Power Bank&r stores 16,000 FE, surplus in, supply back out, exactly what a solar base needs to see the night through.",
    "",
    "Two tricks worth knowing: it charges items placed in its output slot, and it &lkeeps its charge when broken&r. A full bank in a backpack is a power line you can carry to a site that has nothing yet.",
    "",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/stellaris/power_bank.png width:160 height:160 align:center}",
  ],
  "quest.07F94736A736253E.quest_desc": [
    "Ordinary farmland is dead weight off Earth, a crop will not grow and cannot even be planted without air. The &6Space Farm&r ignores all of that and grows on its own internal clock.",
    "",
    "Set it up in pairs: right-click one with dirt, right-click a neighbor with a water bucket, and every dirt farm around the water one turns into farmland. Plant with a seed, harvest with a hoe, it even replants itself.",
    "",
    "A row of these is a fully automatic farm on the Moon.",
    "",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/stellaris/space_farm.png width:160 height:160 align:center}",
  ],
  "quest.36862D1C576AB952.title": "The Program Endures",
  "quest.538E11C948B4BB25.quest_subtitle": "Titanium, the backbone",
  "quest.34920FBD01F40072.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Luna Shadow&r hunts in the lunar forests after dark. It is fast, it is quiet, and it is the reason a night walk in the lunar woods is a bad idea.",
    "",
    "Bring a real weapon, the light hits bounce off. Hunt one to mark it off the Company's ledger.",
  ],
  "quest.04229666DE83F5D1.quest_desc": [
    "Titanium forges into a full tool set, sword included, that sits right between iron and diamond: 1,200 durability, 6.0 mining speed, 14 enchantability.",
    "",
    "Not required for the mission, but a titanium pickaxe is a nice way to make the ore pay for its own excavation.",
  ],
  "quest.72BB2D762D384F85.title": "Regolith Survey",
  "quest.407BDA43FF92727D.quest_desc": [
    "A space station is not built block by block, it is &lplanned&r. The recipe for the plan is paper and titanium: four sheets around an ingot make a blank &6Space Station Blueprint&r.",
    "",
    "In the Engineering Station's &6Space Station Planner&r tab, pick one of the three station sizes, lay the eight required materials in the grid with the blank blueprint beside them, press the button once to check and again to plan. The planned blueprint comes out ready to fly.",
  ],
  "quest.283008E69A58F4EF.quest_desc": [
    "At the bottom of the deep lab sits the &6Heart of Luna&r - 550 health, swollen with every colonist it took. It refuses to fall at two points in the fight until it has answered back, it turns aside blows and arrows aimed at its face, and its roar doubles its damage and leaves infection hanging in the air.",
    "",
    "Its ray is what kills. Strike from behind, never stand in the cloud, and do not let the fight outlast your oxygen.",
    "",
    "Doctor Vey carried the last of her vaccine down here to end it at the source. She did not come back up. Finish her mission.",
  ],
  "quest.5DB0AEE06DE7C6FF.title": "Wiring the Grid",
  "quest.11470E8D528AC363.title": "A Toehold With Air",
  "quest.03A014D7C04B8F3E.title": "Semiconductor Grade",
  "quest.1FBB699895BACDE6.quest_desc": [
    "Every Stellaris machine drinks the same energy, FE, and the cheapest tap we have is the &6Coal Generator&r. Feed it coal, charcoal or coal blocks and it pushes 3 FE per tick into whatever touches it.",
    "",
    "It holds a 48,000 FE buffer, so it keeps working between refills. One piece of coal is worth roughly 530 FE; a block, about ten times that.",
    "",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/stellaris/coal_generator.png width:160 height:160 align:center}",
  ],
  "quest.60A282BD8C9F15D4.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Cargo Unloader&r stands next to a pad and does the unpacking: when a lander touches down within 5 blocks, it pulls everything out, rocket and fuel slots first, then the cargo, at one stack per second.",
    "",
    "It spends 100 FE per stack and only looks for a new lander once its own 30 slots are emptied, so clear it out between flights.",
    "",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/stellaris/cargo_unloader.png width:160 height:160 align:center}",
  ],
  "quest.726DA92B721D8145.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Oil Finder Module&r mounts the survey tool on the helmet and never wears out, unlike the handheld version.",
    "",
    "Its three tiers trade width for precision: 5x5 chunks scanned around you, 3x3, or 1x1. A wider scan drains the helmet battery faster; a narrower one tells you exactly which chunk to drill.",
    "",
    "Same battery as night vision, charge at a power bank or a solar panel's item slot.",
  ],
  "quest.6522EC06CDD60743.title": "Rations to Go",
  "quest.7F6D18BE0C43473A.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click with the vaccine and it does two things at once: clears the infection you are already carrying, and makes you &lpermanently immune&r, parasites can never put it in you again.",
    "",
    "Use it before the research is done and it only tells you that you are not ready. With the injection read, the Moon stops being a hazard zone and becomes a workplace.",
  ],
  "quest.2045DBD6D4235282.title": "We Are Not Alone",
  "quest.538133FC5D656547.title": "Drilling the Deposit",
  "quest.53EA03FE1CC9FC20.title": "Impact Sites",
  "quest.52877BB0A9B1CD91.title": "The Other Kind of Village",
  "quest.46C06EC4085C06DA.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Oxygen Propagator&r extends a distributor's reach. Standing inside an already-covered zone and powered, it adds its own 3x3 chunks to the fillable area, and air there does not count against the distributor's own budget.",
    "",
    "Chain them along a corridor or across a station wing and the sealed space grows with no total limit. An unpowered one adds nothing, so budget the FE.",
    "",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/stellaris/oxygen_propagator.png width:160 height:160 align:center}",
  ],
  "quest.5289EAB23C1BBA9C.title": "Specimen Containment",
  "quest.2CBA0B7B5FB779D1.title": "&bStellaris: From Earth to the Stars",
  "quest.51E79322BBADB786.title": "Trees That Shouldn't Be",
  "quest.772596DD6F46294E.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Blender&r crushes up to nine ingredient types into a new product. Wire it to the grid, drop materials anywhere in its 3x3 grid and press &6Blend&r, it never starts on its own, so nothing parked in the grid gets eaten by accident.",
    "",
    "It also works as a powered shapeless crafting table: every shapeless recipe runs here, plus its own. One press batches as much as the result slot can hold.",
  ],
  "quest.538E11C948B4BB25.quest_desc": [
    "Everything we fly is built on titanium. The ore hides below Y=32 in the Overworld, deepslate layers included, and, as it turns out, on the Moon as well.",
    "",
    "Dig some up and bring back &6Raw Titanium&r. It smelts or blasts like any other ore: one chunk becomes one ingot.",
  ],
  "quest.67B4306849958734.quest_desc": [
    "Two modules belong only to the rover: the &6Tank Module&r doubles the fuel cell to 6,000 mB, and the &6Speed Module&r multiplies top speed by 1.5.",
    "",
    "Both live in Moon Sphere loot, alongside the cargo module and hydrogen motor the rover shares with the rocket. Install them at the Upgrade tab like everything else, and empty the tank before swapping motors.",
  ],
  "quest.42AE42F63D04D8C7.title": "Wreck of the Transport",
  "task.5F3BA847E2E1BDEC.title": "Scan chunks until one reads oil",
  "quest.6E978651BF338940.quest_desc": [
    "Before trusting the system on the Moon, prove it at home: box in a room, power the distributor, feed it oxygen, and read the status line in its GUI.",
    "",
    "If it refuses, the message tells you why, sky leak, room too large, no oxygen, no energy. Fix what it names and it goes green. Once a room breathes, torches, crops and people all work inside it.",
  ],
  "quest.43D44D7FC031A761.title": "Free Light, Slow Light",
  "quest.664B2D0030C54D75.title": "Metal From the Sky",
  "quest.6054CF817A8BED89.title": "Making Orbit Livable",
  "quest.2FC0E94A3C2F4AD7.title": "Ignition",
  "quest.726DA92B721D8145.title": "The Helm That Sees Oil",
  "quest.2673F444580FB511.quest_desc": [
    "The bare suit stops nothing, the &6Damage Protection Module&r is what makes it armor. Tier 1 gives a piece iron's worth, tier 2 diamond's, tier 3 netherite's.",
    "",
    "Each module covers a single piece, so a full set takes four. Install them as budget allows: helmet and chestplate first, where the hits land.",
  ],
  "quest.6C561ECCEE2F268A.quest_desc": [
    "The chestplate carries the suit's propellant: a &6Diesel Tank Module&r or &6Hydrogen Tank Module&r - 1,000, 2,000 or 3,000 mB by tier, feeds whatever the boots burn.",
    "",
    "Fill it with a bucket or a fluid cell of the matching fluid. Pick one fuel and stay with it; a tank only holds one kind at a time.",
  ],
  "quest.52877BB0A9B1CD91.quest_desc": [
    "Not every village up here kept its people. The &6destroyed villages&r stand as they were left, and their streets belong to &6Parasite Villagers&r, what is left of the colonists.",
    "",
    "They do not hunt; they strike back at whoever hurts them first, and every hit infects for 16 seconds and slows for 4. Wounded past 70% they can evolve after about two minutes into something that does hunt, finish them cleanly or leave them alone.",
    "",
    "Killing one sometimes lets a lunar parasite crawl out of the corpse. Check the houses for loot and SD cards anyway.",
  ],
  "quest.62FD87644F52AFFF.title": "Brain in a Shell",
  "quest.604EF496D82872ED.title": "The Old Footprint",
  "quest.1AC6C0AFAEAF8E2C.quest_desc": [
    "&6Moon Berries&r grow on vines hanging through the forest biomes, and they carry a special distinction: they are the one food the book lists as &ledible in space&r, no can required.",
    "",
    "An arrow through the vine knocks them down. A handy snack for the long walk home, most other food still wants a pressurized room or a can.",
  ],
  "quest.41756307A29CB444.title": "Wheels for the Desert",
  "quest.2FC0E94A3C2F4AD7.quest_desc": [
    "Ten seconds of noise and the ground falls away. The ship climbs until the planet stops being a place and becomes a map, then the destination screen offers the choice: Earth Orbit or the Moon.",
    "",
    "Wherever we point first, the ship does the flying. Landing is the lander's job, and it is not gentle unless we made it so.",
  ],
  "quest.29DD1B7695C09410.quest_subtitle": "All four, or none",
  "quest.570B5ADAB67AF834.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Electrolyzer&r breaks water into the two gases the program runs on: &6oxygen&r to breathe and &6hydrogen&r to burn. Feed it water from the pump, or a bucket or cell in the second slot, and it works on its own.",
    "",
    "Hydrogen comes out the machine's &lright&r face, oxygen out the &lleft&r, matching the refinery's habit. 10 mB of water becomes 10 mB of hydrogen and 5 mB of oxygen each tick at 50 FE/t.",
    "",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/stellaris/electrolyzer.png width:160 height:160 align:center}",
  ],
  "quest.0D8A53E286DEAA48.quest_subtitle": "Secret quest!? xD",
  "quest.44DF48BE87ACCC94.title": "The Edge of the Sky",
  "quest.513992733EAB2CB4.quest_desc": [
    "Everything modular in the program upgrades the same way: item on the left of the Engineering Station's &6Upgrade&r tab, module in the middle, upgraded item out the right, keeping whatever modules it already had.",
    "",
    "Modules of the same kind replace each other, so installing a higher tier upgrades the old one instead of stacking. Each suit piece takes only the modules built for it: oxygen and scanners on the helmet, tanks on the chestplate, jets on the boots.",
  ],
  "quest.0A0A4FC4C933B5CC.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Laboratory&r is where the infection gets studied instead of suffered. Two tabs: &6Research&r and &6Vaccine&r.",
    "",
    "Feed a filled storage cell into Research and press start: the analysis takes 30 seconds and &lempties the cell whether it succeeds or not&r, so load it deep. Roughly 1, 100, 200, 300, 400 and 500 parasites carry you through stages 0 to 5, each success pays an SD card with another piece of the colony's story.",
    "",
    "Stage 4 names the last vaccine ingredient. Stage 5 only files the paperwork.",
    "",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/stellaris/laboratory.png width:160 height:160 align:center}",
  ],
  "quest.11470E8D528AC363.quest_desc": [
    "Time to unpack the drill from home: power, electrolyzer, distributor. A sealed moon-stone room with green status is the first real base up here, somewhere to stand bare-faced, charge the helmet, let a torch burn.",
    "",
    "Same rules as Earth, higher stakes: seal against the sky, stay inside 3x3 chunks, feed the oxygen. Chain propagators down the corridor if the toehold grows into a station wing.",
  ],
  "task.1D14E42603EAE6C3.title": "Learn where oil hides",
  "quest.607E5DC6C9379AB5.quest_desc": [
    "The Blender turns Moon Stone into &6Moon Stone Dust&r, and two dust plus a coal blend into two silicon, the offworld answer to quartz.",
    "",
    "On a long expedition this is the recipe that keeps the silicon pipeline running without a supply rocket: quarry, grind, blend, print.",
  ],
  "quest.0CBF87DCBCD2CFF0.title": "Offworld Commerce",
  "quest.28F3CBE539F1DD72.quest_desc": [
    "When the surface fell, the survivors dug down and sealed a laboratory complex behind them, and brought the infection inside in someone's blood. The tunnels are still down there: halls, cells, spawning pods, and something at the bottom the smaller parasites answer to.",
    "",
    "Small dungeon entrances hide underground across the Moon; the full complex with its vault sits deeper. Bring light, a shield, and more oxygen than feels necessary.",
    "",
    "The SD cards in these halls are the colony's own record, collect them when the path is clear.",
  ],
  "quest.292BE01E4FC2D031.quest_desc": [
    "The &6evolved&r form is the dangerous one: an infection aura reaching 4 blocks every 1.5 seconds, and attacks that stack Weakness and Slowness on top of the infection.",
    "",
    "Do not fight one unvaccinated if you can help it, and watch your oxygen, these fights run long.",
  ],
  "quest.1AD93FB86F93CCB6.title": "The Four Ingredients",
  "quest.60A282BD8C9F15D4.title": "Ground Crew",
  "quest.1F01BFA19F649CB9.title": "A Waypoint in Space",
  "quest.79CFFAB71C2DE2E3.quest_subtitle": "Only exists here",
  "quest.36A23E238E3B1C77.quest_desc": [
    "&6Blue Fish&r swim the Lunar Blue Lake biome and nowhere else, peaceful little swimmers, three to seven to a school.",
    "",
    "They drop &6Blue Plasma&r, an ingredient of the vaccine and the heart of the Star Light Panel. Harvest a few while you are there.",
  ],
  "quest.0CBF87DCBCD2CFF0.quest_desc": [
    "Alien merchants stock their own lists, the coin is familiar but the goods are not. Thirteen professions, thirteen catalogs, all drawn from lunar life.",
    "",
    "Make one trade to mark the first business deal ever closed off Earth. The farmers, the masons and the librarians are the interesting stalls.",
  ],
  "quest.1E9E1E6667BB63BA.title": "Three Rows of Hold",
  "quest.23EAB6035BA4C48D.title": "Working in the Black",
  "task.48A319C5BC0F2B22.title": "Check a station plan's material list",
  "quest.40F165367B9F6088.title": "The Parts Bin",
  "quest.4D35E1719A092E9E.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click the &6Autopilot Module&r in hand to pick a destination, then install it. From then on the rocket flies straight there without opening the destination screen.",
    "",
    "The better reason to want one: an autopiloted ship brings its lander down &lgently&r. No crater, no broken legs, the landing that does not have to be survived first.",
  ],
  "task.5749FAA2D2919DAE.title": "Install a module at the Upgrade Station",
  "quest.62FD87644F52AFFF.quest_desc": [
    "&6Lunar Parasites&r spawn all over the Moon, more underground than above it. They latch on, and what they leave behind is the &6Infection&r.",
    "",
    "Honey burns them, cold slows them, and killing one drops a &6Parasite&r the Laboratory can bank. That is the raw material of the cure.",
  ],
  "quest.29DD1B7695C09410.quest_desc": [
    "The Space Suit is the difference between an expedition and a funeral: helmet, chestplate, leggings and boots, copper and titanium the whole way.",
    "",
    "Wear &lall four pieces&r or the suit counts for nothing, three pieces protect you from nothing at all.",
    "",
    "Out of the box the suit is an empty shell: it blocks no damage and carries no air. Modules, installed only at the Engineering Station's Upgrade tab, are what turn it into life support. The suit itself is repaired with titanium.",
  ],
  "quest.0752B5D72A823293.title": "A Bare Ship Only Flies",
  "quest.36A23E238E3B1C77.title": "Something's Fishy",
  "quest.56240DD5B0414A39.title": "Know Your Neighbors",
  "quest.7025C5AC5860603E.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Oil Finder&r reports the exact amount of oil under your feet, right-clicked anywhere: green for a rich deposit, orange for a thin one, red for nothing.",
    "",
    "It holds a 1,000 FE battery and spends 1 FE per scan, recharge it in the item slot of a generator or power bank. Each scan also costs durability, so it will eventually wear out. Later, a helmet module scans continuously without ever breaking.",
  ],
  "quest.61D18A8A3B470E32.title": "What They Became",
  "task.10074C661498E27F.title": "Carry a planned blueprint to Earth Orbit and press Build Space Station",
  "quest.41756307A29CB444.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Rover&r is the program's truck: iron, titanium, a cable, a bucket and redstone on the crafting table, then diesel in the fuel slot - 3,000 mB of tank that stretches one bucket a very long way at 1 mB per 25 blocks.",
    "",
    "Two seats, one row of cargo, and a horn's worth of momentum: a rover at speed hurts what it hits. Sneak-punch the empty rover to pack it up again, it keeps fuel and modules, but drops its cargo.",
    "",
    "Its modules come out of Moon Sphere chests: a tank doubler, a speed module, plus the cargo module and hydrogen motor it shares with the rocket.",
  ],
  "quest.6522EC06CDD60743.quest_desc": [
    "Empty cans come in all sixteen dye colors and can be recolored later, so the galley can stay color-coded: green for vegetables, red for meat, whatever keeps the crew honest.",
    "",
    "Craft a couple of small cans, iron nuggets and dye, and fill them at the Vacuumator before the first flight. Sixteen colors, two sizes, zero excuses to starve in vacuum.",
  ],
  "quest.62857711BE7CB286.title": "A Battery With Legs",
  "quest.7FCD49FEAE1EAB87.title": "Eyes in the Dark",
  "quest.12058BED6DA0F944.title": "Stockpile the Hull Metal",
  "quest.407BDA43FF92727D.title": "Drawing the Station",
  "task.284B75A71BBF458B.title": "Read the mission briefing",
  "quest.6F973629788228BA.quest_desc": [
    "This is the workbench of the whole program. Everything we fly, drive or wear is built or upgraded here, across three tabs.",
    "",
    "&6Rocket Station&r lays out rocket parts and hands back a ship. &6Upgrade Station&r bolts modules onto the rocket, the rover and the space suit, the only way modules install. &6Space Station Planner&r turns a blueprint plus materials into a station in orbit.",
    "",
    "Craft it from diamonds, titanium, a crafting table and silicon. Clear floor space, this one earns a permanent spot.",
    "",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/stellaris/craftrocket.png width:160 height:160 align:center click_action:none:}",
  ],
  "quest.44DF48BE87ACCC94.quest_subtitle": "Earth Orbit",
  "quest.283008E69A58F4EF.title": "End It at the Source",
  "quest.40F165367B9F6088.quest_desc": [
    "A rocket is four kinds of part. The &6Nose Cone&r pierces the sky, four &6Fins&r keep the flight straight, and the &6Engine&r, iron blocks, redstone and titanium, does the lifting.",
    "",
    "The body itself is nothing but titanium ingots arranged at assembly. Forge one cone, four fins and an engine now; the ingots come when we build.",
  ],
  "quest.0D8A53E286DEAA48.title": "The Next Dot on the Map",
  "quest.7025C5AC5860603E.title": "The Sniffer",
  "quest.7714D18235F1B346.title": "Stacking the Ship",
  "quest.51E79322BBADB786.quest_desc": [
    "Someone or something planted a forest up here. &6Lunar Logs&r strip and plank like any wood, a full set exists, signs and boats included, and the planks have that pale dead-world look no stain gives you on Earth.",
    "",
    "Grab a log for the collection. A lunar boat, by the way, floats on the blue lakes fine.",
  ],
  "quest.513992733EAB2CB4.title": "The Upgrade Tab",
  "quest.67B4306849958734.title": "Tricking Out the Truck",
  "quest.36862D1C576AB952.quest_desc": [
    "Read it back: oil wells mapped, fuel cracked, a ship stacked and flown, two worlds visited, a station raised in orbit, the deep lab's heart silenced, and the infection answered with a vaccine.",
    "",
    "What was left of the last program, the sphere, the colonies, the logs, we found, learned from and finished. The Moon is a workplace now, not a warning.",
    "",
    "The Company does not close programs; it extends them. Keep the pad clear, keep the cells loaded, and watch the sky for the next destination marker.",
  ],
  "quest.43D44D7FC031A761.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Solar Panel&r never asks for fuel, only a clear view of the sky. One FE per tick is little, but it never sleeps while the sun is up.",
    "",
    "It also has an item slot that charges equipment at 10 FE/t, ten times its own output. That slot is how we will feed the Oil Finder and the suit helmet later.",
    "",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/stellaris/solar_panel.png width:160 height:160 align:center}",
  ],
  "quest.5792B04C4FC884A4.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Hydrogen Motor&r swaps the rocket's engine from refined Fuel to the hydrogen the electrolyzer already makes, cutting oil out of the flight loop entirely.",
    "",
    "Two warnings. Empty the fuel tank before installing: a tank holds one fluid at a time. And the motor is the priciest module, diamond and desh blocks, unless a Moon dungeon chest hands one over first. It also fits the rover.",
  ],
  "quest.36E29BBF361EF35B.quest_desc": [
    "The last crew left their story in chests: &6SD Cards&r holding evacuation orders, research logs, colonist diaries and black-box entries. Satellites and operation bases on Earth, meteors, and on the Moon the villages, the sphere, the dungeons and the dead stations.",
    "",
    "Read them in the tablet's SD Card Reader, in order they tell what happened up here. The laboratory's research stages pay one per success too, if you prefer the archive route.",
  ],
  "quest.7778B652D37F72FD.title": "The Sphere",
  "quest.28F3CBE539F1DD72.title": "The Deep Lab",
  "quest.6054CF817A8BED89.quest_desc": [
    "A station hull is the address, not the home. Two machines make it livable: an &6Oxygen Distributor&r pressurizes the rooms (sealed, as always), and the &6Gravity Manipulator&r gives a whole chunk Earth-normal footing, dial it anywhere from 0 to 20 m/s² while powered.",
    "",
    "The manipulator wants desh and a redstone block, and several in one chunk average their settings. With air, gravity and an antenna, the station stops being a project and starts being a place.",
    "",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/stellaris/gravity_manipulator.png width:160 height:160 align:center}",
  ],
  "quest.52DD11B192F6C7D9.title": "Five Kinds of Gray",
  "quest.6E978651BF338940.title": "First Breath Offworld",
  "quest.1AC6C0AFAEAF8E2C.title": "Fruit of the Vines",
  "quest.52860AE90D8D294A.title": "One Small Step",
  "quest.5DB0AEE06DE7C6FF.quest_desc": [
    "Machines farther than a block from the generator still want power. &6Cables&r carry it, up to 20 FE per tick, between anything that holds a buffer.",
    "",
    "Two rules worth memorizing: cables move energy, never fluids; and every machine keeps its own private pool, so it keeps running a while after the wire is cut. Craft a bundle of eight now.",
    "",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/stellaris/cable.png width:160 height:160 align:center}",
  ],
  "quest.78388E872EEB99B4.quest_desc": [
    "This Quest has been authored by &6AllTheMods Staff&r, or a &2Community contributor&r for use in AllTheMods Modpacks. \n\nAs all &6AllTheMods&r packs are licensed under &eAll Rights Reserved&r, this Quest is not allowed to be used in any public packs not released by &6AllTheMods Team&r without explicit permission.\n\nThis quest is intentionally hidden, if you're seeing this, you're in editing mode.",
  ],
  "quest.33A8B5BC07C075FB.quest_desc": [
    "&6Fuel&r is the one the rocket drinks, one launch costs 1,000 mB and a rocket tank holds 3,000 mB, so every bucket here is a third of a full tank.",
    "",
    "&6Diesel&r, the other half of the refinery's output, is for the ground: it feeds the diesel generator and, later, the rover. Keep the two straight, a tank holds one fluid at a time.",
  ],
  "quest.36CCF8C0A1B62260.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Fuel Refinery&r is where oil becomes the mission. Powered and fed, it splits 10 mB of oil per tick into &6Fuel&r and &6Diesel&r at once, five and five.",
    "",
    "The two products leave through different faces: Fuel exits the machine's &lright&r side, Diesel the &lleft&r. Plan the pipework around that, or pull each out with cells in their own slots.",
    "",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/stellaris/fuel_refinery.png width:160 height:160 align:center}",
  ],
  "quest.03A014D7C04B8F3E.quest_desc": [
    "Two quartz plus a coal in the Blender make three &6Silicon&r. It is the chip inside everything smart the Company builds: the tablet, the oil finder, the antenna, the engineering station.",
    "",
    "Produce nine now, the next machine alone takes a share. Later, on the Moon, rock dust will refine into silicon the same way.",
  ],
  "task.26D5BACFAAFC247E.title": "Complete research stage 4 at the Laboratory",
  "quest.7778B652D37F72FD.quest_desc": [
    "Older than the regolith it sits on: a seamless metal sphere our drills cannot scratch, with aliens trading at its edge, they saw the parasite before and they want none of it.",
    "",
    "Something grew up guarding it. A &6Star Crawler Mother&r circles the structure, 400 health of plated armor and no safe range to fight her from, slow heavy swings beat fast light ones.",
    "",
    "The chests inside are the good stuff: rover modules, the shield module, launch pad towers, rocket modules, blue plasma, canned goods and SD cards. Check every room.",
  ],
  "quest.79CFFAB71C2DE2E3.quest_desc": [
    "&6Desh&r is the reason the Moon matters: a rare metal that forms &lnowhere else in the galaxy&r, hiding below Y=32 in moon rock.",
    "",
    "Mine it for Raw Desh and smelt or blast it like titanium. The ingots go into the program's top shelf, rocket modules, the gravity manipulator, station plans, the strongest generator panels.",
    "",
    "Bring back four chunks now, and remember this ore when the station bill of materials comes due.",
  ],
  "quest.72BB2D762D384F85.quest_desc": [
    "The surface is a builder's quarry: &6Moon Stone&r under everything, pale &6Moon Sand&r in the deserts, and veins of &6Moon Iron Ore&r threaded through the rock, free iron a long way from the nearest furnace of home.",
    "",
    "Moon stone grinds into dust at the Blender, and the dust blends into silicon, on a long stay, the rocks themselves feed the chip supply.",
    "",
    "Collect a piece of each. The whole moon-rock family, bricks, pillars, polished cuts, builds nicely.",
  ],
  "quest.6D7658B44ADF9D32.title": "Everything Has a Buffer",
  "quest.0A599B4386B91DFB.title": "Black Geology",
  "quest.1F01BFA19F649CB9.quest_desc": [
    "An &6Antenna&r turns a launch pad into a registered landing spot, a rocket can aim for it instead of dropping at random coordinates.",
    "",
    "Install it by right-clicking the pad's center; the block directly under the center must be soft, dirt, sand, air, water, moon sand or moon stone. Then open it with an empty hand to name it and set it public or private.",
    "",
    "Private pads take a whitelist: add players to a &6Friends List&r and right-click the antenna with it. Space stations come with an antenna already built in.",
  ],
  "quest.7F6D18BE0C43473A.title": "Immunized",
  "quest.374FC20CBAA68FAB.title": "How This Chapter Works",
  "quest.1AB510AAA30320FF.quest_desc": [
    "The Mother reads the distance and picks her answer: smash up close, charge at range, and a leap from the sky that ends fights. She learns more answers the longer the fight runs.",
    "",
    "Armor plating sheds light hits, so bring the slow heavy weapon and watch for the leap. The trophy and the loot make the fight worth scheduling.",
  ],
  "quest.772596DD6F46294E.title": "The Grinder",
  "task.4B92F458E9359B44.title": "Build a sealed room and read 'Breathable atmosphere'",
  "quest.07F94736A736253E.title": "Farming in Vacuum",
  "quest.1A815140456D89AF.title": "A Place for the Flood",
  "task.30F3400E63D13101.title": "Understand how FE flows",
  "quest.35D032B681A0C5F6.title": "The Bill of Materials",
  "quest.5792B04C4FC884A4.title": "A Cleaner Burn",
  "quest.570B5ADAB67AF834.title": "Splitting Water",
  "task.528B09427E62AB70.title": "Fuel the rocket and clear the sky above the pad",
  "quest.03647D3F914AEF7A.quest_subtitle": "Small steps, big rooms",
  "quest.36E29BBF361EF35B.title": "The Colony's Records",
  "quest.23EAB6035BA4C48D.quest_desc": [
    "Orbit practice worth doing before the big build: stand in open space, watch the oxygen gauge fall, and get a feel for how slowly things drop at half a gravity.",
    "",
    "Nothing to collect, nothing to kill, you, a suit and the planet turning below. Get used to the silence. We will spend real time up here.",
  ],
  "quest.54D4829A316825E7.title": "Plumbing 101",
  "quest.5289EAB23C1BBA9C.quest_desc": [
    "Kill a lunar parasite yourself and it drops a &6Parasite&r, the raw material of the cure. The &6Pathogen Storage Cell&r (amethyst and titanium) banks them: right-click with the cell in hand to load every parasite in your inventory, up to 500.",
    "",
    "One cell, one trip, a full research program in your pocket. The laboratory is going to eat these by the hundred.",
  ],
  "quest.53EA03FE1CC9FC20.quest_desc": [
    "&6Meteorites&r still fall, crashed rock sits in fields and forests, warm to the touch days later by the old reports. The big impact sites hide novite and their own SD cards.",
    "",
    "Read the meteor logs and the infection story starts making an ugly kind of sense: the survey team cracked one open and found threads of something organic inside.",
  ],
  "quest.61D18A8A3B470E32.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Parasite Villagers&r in the destroyed villages are what is left of the colonists. They do not hunt, but they strike back at whoever hurts them first.",
    "",
    "Every hit infects for 16 seconds and slows for 4. Wounded past 70%, one can evolve after a couple of minutes into something that does hunt. Finish them quickly or leave them be.",
  ],
  "quest.15961D434AF37681.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Diesel Generator&r is the strongest engine in the mod: 5 FE per tick burning diesel - 25 FE for every mB, a 10,000 mB tank and a 60,000 FE buffer.",
    "",
    "Feed it by pipe, bucket or cell. One of these holds up a distributor, a propagator and a light or two; real bases grow by adding generators, not by finding a bigger one.",
  ],
  "quest.604EF496D82872ED.quest_desc": [
    "Somewhere in the crater fields stands the &6first landing site&r, the mission that came before ours, flag and all.",
    "",
    "A pilgrimage more than a quest: find it, stand where they stood, and read the ground. The Company likes its crews to know whose footsteps they are walking in.",
  ],
  "quest.33A8B5BC07C075FB.title": "Rocket Grade",
  "task.52D8C541EBDFCA75.title": "AllRightsReserved",
  "quest.607E5DC6C9379AB5.title": "Chips Out of Rocks",
  "quest.3D208516E87A59B1.title": "Reading the Ground",
  "quest.16BF6F4CD96CDA92.title": "The Field Manual",
  "quest.6687660A5F931460.title": "Lunar Extermination",
  "quest.03647D3F914AEF7A.title": "Raising the First Station",
  "quest.283008E69A58F4EF.quest_subtitle": "Doctor Vey's last log",
  "quest.1A815140456D89AF.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Tier 1 Fluid Tank&r stores 5,000 mB of a single fluid, hook it to pipes or fill it with buckets and cells.",
    "",
    "Useful when the refinery outpaces the rocket, or when a water line needs a reservoir between pump and electrolyzer.",
    "",
    "{image:atm:textures/questpics/stellaris/fluid_tank.png width:160 height:160 align:center}",
  ],
  "quest.54D4829A316825E7.quest_desc": [
    "&6Pipes&r move fluids - 250 mB per tick, oil, fuel, diesel, water, oxygen, hydrogen, all of it. Cables will never carry a drop; that is the whole division of labor in this mod.",
    "",
    "&6Fluid Cells&r hold 3,000 mB, three buckets' worth, and leave no empty container behind. They refill machines, tanks, the rocket's fuel slot and even the suit's tanks straight from the hand. Craft eight pipes and three cells.",
  ],
  "quest.3D208516E87A59B1.quest_desc": [
    "Walk a grid and click. One chunk in thirty-two averages out to a find every few minutes of searching, desert and plains are kind to long surveys.",
    "",
    "The moment the bar shows a number instead of nothing, note the coordinates. That chunk is worth real fuel. Confirm it here when you have a deposit marked.",
  ],
  "quest.08D0F5470C27B89B.title": "Light When the Sun Is Down",
  "quest.2CBA0B7B5FB779D1.quest_subtitle": "Home...",
  "quest.229852EBBD2B964A.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Jet Module&r turns the boots into an engine. Tier 1 burns 8 mB of fuel per second and climbs at 0.35 blocks per tick; tier 3 sips 3 mB and climbs at 0.7, higher tiers both last longer and fly better.",
    "",
    "Jet mode toggles between off, normal, hover and elytra. Watch the math: the jet drinks fuel from the chestplate tank &land&r quadruples your oxygen burn while it runs.",
    "",
    "Low gravity plus a jet is the closest thing to teleporting this mod offers.",
  ],
}
